Z||000000||lowCG||07-15-99||04:43 PM||||Does anyone know of anything that'll remove the glue that stays when self-adhesive,velcro has been put on the hard interior parts?<br>I got this car from the Chief of Police,and he'd put radio mounts,velcro,power wires everywhere.
Z||000001||theogre||07-15-99||06:27 PM||||there are several things available at your local home center, K-mart, etc. Goo Gone is one of them.
Z||000002||PaUL||07-15-99||07:40 PM||||Yeah Ive used GooGone before, it works really good. You can also use bug and tar remover.
Z||000003||Dale||07-15-99||08:35 PM||||You can also go to your local paint store and get GOOF OFF.  It works very good but be careful, its a pretty hot mixture.
Z||000004||Bruce||07-15-99||09:06 PM||||I had the same problem with my dash- the previous owner had velcroed an ashtray above the speedometer gauge. After I pulled the velcro off, I used a paint thinner sold for models. It's fairly mild, but still did the job. I Armor-all'd like crazy afterward to get the colors to blend a little. You can't really notice now, unless you look carefully.
Z||000005||lowCG||07-16-99||03:44 AM||||Wow,thanks,will try the mildest first to see if that works,then procede with the stuff that'll possibly melt the dash.<br>I know that bug and tar remover,smells kind of like diesel,will try that first,then Goo Gone,then the toluol stuff,if the other stuff works.<br>Now for that mildew odor that I thought I got rid of...<br>
Z||000006||theogre||07-16-99||02:09 PM||||lysol, or any of the "basin, tub & tile" products will kill midew w/o bleaching the item treated. BT&T will also remove any grease and other dirt, including tobaco soot, from most things. Spray them on and let them stand. spray them again after a few minutes on really heavy things.<p>As for the shredded rag padding used under the carpet,,,, that stuff is nasty. You might never get it cleaned. try pulling the carpet, and spraying both sides good with lysol disinfectant and work it into the carpet side with a brush. hang them in the sun to dry, mildew hates sunlight, and spry them again after they do. Let them dry completely before you reinstall.
Z||000007||PaUL||07-16-99||05:19 PM||||Ive never tried this myself but I read that Oxyfresh mouthwash is good for removing odors. Other deodorizers with reactive oxygen will probably work as well. The oxygen is the single atom kind that easily combines with odor causing molecules. (O not O2).
